            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Unilever sales top forecast as US shoppers drive beauty demand",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: Unilever beat market expectations Thursday (October 23).</p><p>The conglomerate announced third-quarter sales growth over 3% - slightly ahead of forecasts.</p><p>It was largely thanks to consumers buying up its hair care goods like Dove, particularly in North America.</p><p>Strong volume expansion across personal care and beauty drove sales growth of 5.5% in the region.</p><p>Unilever owns many brands, including Ben & Jerry's and Hellmann's mayonnaise.</p><p>The firm wants to push into higher-margin premium products in beauty and personal care.</p><p>It's key to a turnaround plan under new CEO Fernando Fernandez, who took over in March.</p><p>He wants to streamline business, cut costs and explore sales of non-core brands.</p><p>That to boost margins despite weak consumer sentiment and economic uncertainty.</p><p>Unilever's stock has performed better than rival Nestle since Fernandez took over, but underperformed others like Danone and Reckitt.</p><p>Thursday's results comes days after Unilever delayed the spin-off of its Magnum-led ice cream business and blamed it on the U.S. government shutdown.</p><p>It was originally scheduled for November, but still expects to complete the spin-off by year-end.</p><p>Unilever shares were up around 1.5% after the results were announced.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: Unilever beat market expectations Thursday (October 23).</p><p>The conglomerate announced third-quarter sales growth over 3% - slightly ahead of forecasts.</p><p>It was largely thanks to consumers buying up its hair care goods like Dove, particularly in North America.</p><p>Strong volume expansion across personal care and beauty drove sales growth of 5.5% in the region.</p><p>Unilever owns many brands, including Ben & Jerry's and Hellmann's mayonnaise.</p><p>The firm wants to push into higher-margin premium products in beauty and personal care.</p><p>It's key to a turnaround plan under new CEO Fernando Fernandez, who took over in March.</p><p>He wants to streamline business, cut costs and explore sales of non-core brands.</p><p>That to boost margins despite weak consumer sentiment and economic uncertainty.</p><p>Unilever's stock has performed better than rival Nestle since Fernandez took over, but underperformed others like Danone and Reckitt.</p><p>Thursday's results comes days after Unilever delayed the spin-off of its Magnum-led ice cream business and blamed it on the U.S. government shutdown.</p><p>It was originally scheduled for November, but still expects to complete the spin-off by year-end.</p><p>Unilever shares were up around 1.5% after the results were announced.</p></body>",
